    "notes": "Subtests that the runner cannot run outside a browser (testdriver, tentative tests) are skipped for every engine alike. \"Pass rate\" is passed subtests / subtests; \"score\" averages the per-file pass fraction, so large files weigh less. Subtest counts can differ between engines when a test file stops early in one of them: the Subtests column is warpdom's, and each engine's rate is over its own count (jsdom stops early in several WebCryptoAPI files, so it has 176,171 subtests in total to warpdom's 186,857)."
